</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>As a mother stills her child,</l><l>Thou canst hush the ocean wild;</l><l>Boist’rous waves obey Thy will</l><l>When Thou say’st to them, “Be still.”</l><l>Wondrous Sov’reign of the sea,</l><l>Jesus, Savior, pilot me.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Though death’s valley I may pass,</l><l>Still Thy grace will fear surpass;</l><l>In Thy presence I will rest,</l><l>And, while leaning on Thy breast,</l><l>I will hear Thee say to me,</l><l>“Fear not, I will pilot thee.”</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
